#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:86
msgid "Provisioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:88
msgid ""
"|morpheus| automatically seeds MySQL, Redis and RabbitMQ PCF Instance "
"Types, as well as a generic Cloud Foundry Instance Type that will create "
"a shell app used in conjunction with deployments. PCF Marketplace items "
"can also be added to the Provisioning Library in the Cloud detail view "
"Marketplace tab. The Marketplace item will be added to the selected "
"Instance Type and available when selecting the Cloud Foundry Cloud during"
" Instance or App Template creation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:91
msgid "Deployments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:93
msgid ""
"The Cloud Foundry App Instance Type is used in conjunction with "
"deployments. Users do not have to pick deployment when creating a Cloud "
"Foundry App Instance Type, but then Instance will only be a shell of a "
"Cloud Foundry Application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:95
msgid ""
"A deployment in Morpheus can either point to a git hub repository or "
"contain the actual manifest.yml and associated artifacts required for a "
"Cloud Foundry deployment.  During the deployment, Morpheus will gather up"
" the files required.  Therefore, if the deployment points to a git hub "
"repository, Morpheus will fetch the files from git hub.  Once the files "
"are obtained, Morpheus will deploy the artifacts in a similar fashion to "
"the Cloud Foundry cli.  This includes parsing the manifest to obtain the "
"parameters to create or update the Cloud Foundry application.  Morpheus "
"will ignore certain fields such as memory and disk size because they are "
"dictated by the selected plan.  Other fields are utilized such as routes."
"  After parsing the manifest.yml file (including overwriting certain "
"fields), Morpheus is ready to update or create the App in Cloud Foundry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:97
msgid ""
"After the App is configured, the artifacts references in the Morpheus "
"deployment are uploaded to Cloud Foundry for the App.  Note that when "
"paths are referenced in the manifest.yml file, the paths continue to be "
"relative to the manifest.  So, a jar file under build/libs would need to "
"be found under the build/libs directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:99
msgid ""
"If Cloud Foundry services are specified in the manifest, they must "
"already exist within Cloud Foundry.  Morpheus App templates can be "
"utilized to wire up Cloud Foundry services created by Morpheus.  In this "
"case, Morpheus will add all of the included service names defined in the "
"App template to the manifest.yml services section.  Therefore, multiple "
"services can be used and wired up by Morpheus.”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:102
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:104
msgid ""
"To better understand how Morpheus parses the manifest.yml file, lets take"
" a closer look at the Cloud Foundry 'spring-music' project.  The project "
"can be found here (https://github.com/cloudfoundry-samples/spring-music)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:106
msgid ""
"The project contains the required manifest.yml file as well as the source"
" code and build.gradle file to define how the project is to be built.  "
"After downloading the project to your local machine, build the project to"
" generate the jar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:108
msgid "Now, let's take a look at the manifest.yml file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:110
msgid ""
"---\n"
"applications:\n"
"- name: spring-music\n"
"  memory: 1G\n"
"  random-route: true\n"
"  path: build/libs/spring-music.jar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:120
msgid ""
"Using the Cloud Foundry docs (https://docs.cloudfoundry.org/devguide"
"/deploy-apps/manifest.html), we can gain a better understanding of how "
"this file is utilized by Cloud Foundry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:122
msgid ""
"The ``-name`` parameter defines the name that will be given to the "
"application in Cloud Foundry.  Morpheus will overwrite this value with "
"the name given to the Instance being created in Morpheus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:124
msgid ""
"The ``-memory`` parameter (as well as the disk_quota parameter if "
"specified) will be overwritten by Morpheus based on the plan specified "
"for the Instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:126
